;"><em><span style=3D"font-size: 12px;">A Vogue editor plays on a claw mach=
ine at a fashion event in Sydney, Australia. (Photo by Mark Metcalfe/Getty =
Images for Vaefno)</span></em></span></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">And in the center of this unexpected industry=
 is a generation of players and operators who treat claw machines not as ga=
mes, but as engines for making money.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><strong>The kids who never grew out of it</st=
rong></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Before claw machines were content, before the=
y were side hustles, before they were tropes in TikTok videos, they were ev=
erywhere and irresistible to <strong>Erik Kane</strong>.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">=E2=80=9CI remember always seeing them in the=
 early 2000s growing up,=E2=80=9D says Kane, the 26-year-old creator behind=
 the YouTube account <a   href=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/=
d2q-Vf04/VVBCQ82QCH8lF6vjVJwtQX3W1FPBGm5J8y-jN11fKWg2-ZW0W69sMD-6lZ3p7W4Z9f=
j36VHm1hN4J3JWDD-8wGW2L7kC03PggVnW61rKVB8QnyVdW7g14r56RwzDyVThWcM6KsP6ZW5JX=
xjK7tsqHPW5wR3bP4pGdksW30Ty1K48j263N85XTlQTyc3cW2t0HYr5Y92s6W737KnC6WBX5tW1=
3dHc37WHzTBW3T0Bgf6K2vhGW1_3Qw_5lZ-PrW2NtG4S2chzHBW1qWR0t7vKDpPW3qy_C-8sx3K=
2VQ7mmW1n4zRrW1s5dCh2nvjjwf4mc8-W04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-i=
d=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"9h1RCX5+" target=3D"_blank">Arcade Warrior</a=
>. =E2=80=9CThere was always one in a grocery store, restaurant, mall. They=
 were very prevalent. The marquee sign would light up next to flashing ligh=
ts, plus the claw itself. I was always drawn to it.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">As a kid in Rochester, New York, Kane begged =
his parents for a dollar to play. "If it was not for them giving me a dolla=
r to play whenever I would see one, I probably never would have gotten full=
y invested in them," he says. Eventually, he started filming. Today, his ch=
annel has <strong>2m+ </strong>subscribers.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">=E2=80=9CAround the time I was 12 or 13, I st=
arted to film some clips of me just playing,=E2=80=9D he says. =E2=80=9CMe =
and my brother would go around and film but wouldn=E2=80=99t upload anythin=
g. It was just something we did for fun.=E2=80=9D</p></div></div></td></tr>=
</tbody></table>
