e=3D"rich_text"><p style=3D"line-height:125%"><span style=3D"color: #192733=
;"><em><span style=3D"font-size: 12px;">Erik Kane shows off his latest plus=
hie prize. (YouTube)</span></em></span></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">In Pennsylvania, future YouTuber <strong>Matt=
 Magnone</strong>, known online as <a href=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t=
/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVBCQ82QCH8lF6vjVJwtQX3W1FPBGm5J8y-jN11fKV-2-ZW0W5BW0B=
06lZ3pGW84BnbK5snlvcW17FcWh6K1pD0W7pwM8R144pKcN463L7KzZrLvW83c6ZQ2BV902W7NT=
-X31PYqw8W66k8C64sY_8tW9lQPwL3QYKgnVs--Sm4mmlPZW4nC5zL6WnFc6W87vwcC8_Hvx_W2=
01H7d1lrRVdN1h73DRmx9KqW24ytQZ6GwFB4N8tt1N9zR6npW4FhDdR3kL14-N7rthjQWlBQ8N5=
XbPJWTCHC0f5v_LyT04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-=
link-id-v2=3D"hEHwuuwa" target=3D"_blank">Arcade Matt</a>, was doing the sa=
me thing.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">=E2=80=9CEver since I was a little kid, it wa=
s the one game at the arcade that you could win an instant gift with,=E2=80=
=9D says the 38-year-old. =E2=80=9CInstant gratification=E2=80=94millennial=
s love that. I didn=E2=80=99t care what the prize was. It was just the fact=
 that I could win something.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">At 17, he bought a full-size claw machine for=
 $500, which he stored in his mom=E2=80=99s basement and practiced on daily=
.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">=E2=80=9CMy first job was a cashier at a neig=
hborhood pharmacy and I only made $5 an hour so I had to save up for months=
 and months and months in my pretzel jar until I finally had enough money t=
o buy it,=E2=80=9D he says.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">He now has <strong>1.83m </strong>YouTube sub=
scribers, who he fondly refers to as goobers.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Alongside the channels, the competitive claw =
machine community has grown. Aspiring clawmasters share tips and tricks onl=
ine. Clawcades host tournaments for local players. The cost to play depends=
 on location and prizes, but on average is still between a quarter and $2 p=
er play. They=E2=80=99re especially popular in Japan, where a woman named Y=
uka Nakajima holds the Guinness World Record for most claw-machine wins at =
3.5k.</p></div></div></td></tr></tbody></table>
<div id=3D"hs_cos_wrapper_module-2-0-5" class=3D"hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrap=
